c(45, "§8.1 table (verbatim); §8.1; part 8 #1", "must-have", "§8.1 immediate fix — repair the App Store listing (verbatim): " + table("## 8.1 Immediate fix", 0) + " — replace the dead support address (help@thelastingchange.com already works); remove 'Payment is charged to your App Store account' or sell through IAP; put real amounts, periods and trial length under the pricing heading; replace 'cancel anytime in account settings' with the real route or build it — 'the cheapest item in Part 8 and the one with the most direct evidence'.", "listing states a rail, a cancel path and a support address that are all false", "blocked-conversion", "4 defects, each with a reviewer who hit it", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11375486586", "11605113507", "12822274987", "12320369125", "11594706487", "11736211586"], "", "")

c(46, "§8.2; part 8 #2", "must-have", "§8.2 immediate fix — put a cancel control in the app and on the web: zero reviews in 1080 days describe a working in-app or web cancel control; a self-service Cancel subscription control in the account screen and on /manage-subscription with on-screen and email confirmation; account deletion must end billing, and deleting data must not lock out a period already paid for; 'the only change that deals with all of the top five 1★ drivers — no path, email-only, ignored requests, charges after cancellation, and charges after deletion'.", "no cancel control anywhere", "1★-burst", "cancel_friction 51 / 29.14%; NO_PATH 27; EMAIL_ONLY 12; AFTER_CANCEL 12; AFTER_DELETE 5", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11594706487", "11736211586", "11101438874", "13219619467", "12431464017"], "", "")

c(47, "§8.3; part 8 #3", "product-rule", "§8.3 immediate fix — make the subscription an explicit, separate, opt-in line at checkout: show the book and the subscription as separate lines with amount, period and renewal date; default the subscription to off — a book-only option must never produce a recurring charge; show the full total on a final confirmation step before charging and state any post-purchase upsell as an additional charge; include the recurring terms in the order confirmation email ('It's such a small change to your email template'); the disclosure requests come from the people harmed (REQ_DISCLOSURE 4, all 1★).", "app subscription bundled by default with a physical-goods checkout", "1★-burst", "TIED_TO_BOOK 43; consent_failure 56; NO_CONSENT 36 (all 1★); DESELECTED 1; CHECKOUT_TRICK 5; REQ_DISCLOSURE 4", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13710163306", "13599501333", "12865205440", "11018581118", "12320369125", "12437954281"], "", "")

c(48, "§8.4; part 8 #4", "must-have", "§8.4 immediate fix — send renewal notices and use a recognisable billing descriptor: a pre-renewal email before every charge naming the product, the amount and a one-click cancel link; a card descriptor that reads LASTING CHANGE, not a sibling app's name (Effecto, Walking Yoga) or the legal entity (Medical Score).", "no renewal notice; descriptor is a sibling app or the corporate name", "1★-burst", "NO_NOTICE 11; SURPRISE_CHARGE 17; UNKNOWN_DESCRIPTOR 5; BLOCKED_CARD 7", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13728916762", "13434418762", "11025658129", "13630518203", "13688126203"], "", "")

c(49, "§8.5; part 8 #5", "tactic", "§8.5 experiment — refund first-charge disputes and measure public damage: REFUND_REFUSED 36 (all 1★), 12 shielded by terms, TRUST_ESCALATED 16, TRUST_WARN_OTHERS 67 (the largest code); several asked for a refund on the same day as the charge and were refused; for a window, refund any charge disputed shortly after renewal and any charge after a documented cancellation, then compare new 1★ volume, chargebacks and warning text — 'the current policy produces the most-repeated public warning'.", "refuse-by-default refunds", "1★-burst", "REFUND_REFUSED 36 / 1.00★; same-day refusals 3; WARN_OTHERS 67", "research", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11149347868", "11533637208", "13630518203", "10644767233"], "", "")

c(50, "§8.6; §8.6 pure-product table (verbatim); §8.6 request table (verbatim); part 8 #6", "insight", "§8.6 research question — is the app worth paying for on its own? Not one review subscribes because of something the app does; outcomes 10 vs money harm 115; the only pure product signal is 14 reviews criticising the app with no money problem (verbatim): " + table("## 8.6 Research question", 0) + " — two threads, both arguing for fewer inputs not more features: input burden (APP_COMPLEX 10, all US — split check-ins through the day, ask questions instead of showing empty fields) and thin value per input ('pen and paper', 'glorified tracker'); research: a guided time-of-day check-in flow vs the current logging screen, measuring 7-day retention; 11 requests total, none voiced more than four times — no basis for committing to any feature (verbatim): " + table("## 8.6 Research question", 1), "daily long-form self-report; presets only", "complaint", "pure-product 14 / 1.43★; COMPLEX 10; SHALLOW 13; requests 11 across 8 codes", "research", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12234895585", "10935045789", "10945514507", "11403481792", "11811397305", "12745524191", "10406065131", "11533637208", "12209394949"], "", "a data-hungry tracker must give back more than it asks")

c(51, "§8.7; part 8 #7", "must-never-break", "§8.7 immediate fix — login and account state: DEF_LOGIN 14 (8.00%, all but one 1★), in the first review and still in Era 3 — 'account registration is not complete' after payment; 'account doesn't exist'; no create-account path on the sign-in screen; login forgotten on a poor network; every successful web payment must end in a usable app account, linked by the purchase email, with account creation and email-link recovery on the sign-in screen; 'my email is not even registered. Then why was I even charged' shows two systems disagreeing about who the customer is.", "web purchase and app account not linked", "1★-burst", "DEF_LOGIN 14 / 8.00% / 1.07★", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11470336869", "11583091379", "12262018303", "12539621585", "11339754455", "12858676123"], "", "")

